So, how can we get a single integer which solves all three of these congruences at the same time?

31:50.060 --> 31:55.060
So, here, n1 is 7, n2 is 19, n3 is 13, is 3, rather,

31:55.900 --> 32:01.600
which makes m1 19 times 3, m2 7 times 3, m3 7 times 19.

32:01.980 --> 32:08.160
So, it's like, it's missing the 3, it's missing the 19, it's missing the 7, yeah.

32:08.780 --> 32:11.740
Anyway, so we get 57, 21, and 133.

32:12.740 --> 32:17.460
Again, I'm just identifying a1 as 3, a2 as 10, a3 as 6.

32:17.520 --> 32:21.440
We won't use these again until the, uh, towards the end of the solution.

32:21.960 --> 32:23.020
So, first order of business,

32:23.880 --> 32:27.880
what's m bar 1 inverse in z7?

