What's the inverse of 2 in z19?

32:52.000 --> 32:55.520
Well, I didn't know that right off, so I decided to go back to our method.

32:55.840 --> 32:58.100
We go 19, 2 is a, b,

32:58.900 --> 33:00.680
divide, leaves me a remainder of 1.

