So, the Euclidean, vector Euclidean algorithm was kind of short-lived here, wasn't it?

33:06.560 --> 33:08.620
I got to what I needed in the second step.

33:08.620 --> 33:11.460
I got 9 minus 9b equal to 1,

33:11.540 --> 33:15.120
which gives me 1 is 19 minus 9 times 2.

33:15.920 --> 33:19.140
In other words, 2 bar inverse is equal to minus 9.

33:19.140 --> 33:20.920
But, we're working in z19.

33:21.540 --> 33:23.900
So, if I add 19 to that, I get 10.

33:24.720 --> 33:29.460
So, 2 inverse is equal to 10 in z19, at which point I was like,

33:30.320 --> 33:31.540
oh, duh.

33:31.540 --> 33:34.580
Of course, 2 times 10 is 20, and 20 is 1.

33:35.040 --> 33:36.540
Of course, it's 2.

33:37.200 --> 33:39.160
Of course, the inverse of 2 is 10, right?

33:39.340 --> 33:41.300
But, I needed this calculation to see it.

33:41.340 --> 33:41.780
You know, I did.

33:42.580 --> 33:44.860
So, d2 is 10, because that's the number

33:44.860 --> 33:50.060
whose equivalence class, mod 19, is the inverse of 2.

33:50.720 --> 33:50.960
Alright?

33:53.000 --> 33:57.320
And then, what's m3 inverse in z3?

33:57.320 --> 34:02.940
133 bar is just 1, so again, d3 is 1.

34:03.140 --> 34:06.120
So, these, the 1, d1 and d3 are kind of boring.

34:06.240 --> 34:07.780
Only d2 was interesting here.

34:08.540 --> 34:10.320
So, we go back to the proof.

34:10.440 --> 34:12.660
We assemble the solution as in star in the proof.

34:13.600 --> 34:17.740
And, so, we got a1, m1, d1, plus a2, m2, d2, plus a3, m3, d3.

34:18.220 --> 34:19.640
Put the pieces together here.

34:19.640 --> 34:31.420
We had 3 times 57, times 1, 10, times 21, times 10, and 6 times 133, times 1.

34:32.440 --> 34:35.780
And, that gives me 3,069.

34:36.320 --> 34:40.940
But, we're working mod 399, so I can subtract off a bit of that.

34:41.160 --> 34:43.820
And, that is congruent to 276.

34:45.040 --> 34:45.980
And, so, there you go.

34:45.980 --> 34:52.640
So, that's 276, x equals 276, simultaneously solves all three of the given congruences.

34:53.160 --> 34:54.780
And, you can check your answer.

34:55.120 --> 34:56.520
I mean, I checked my answer down here.

34:57.800 --> 34:58.960
Here it is, you know.

34:59.940 --> 35:02.360
276 is congruent to 3 because of this.

35:03.340 --> 35:06.400
276 is congruent to 10 mod 9 because of that equation.

35:07.620 --> 35:13.740
276 is congruent to 6 mod 3 because these are both congruent to 0 mod 3.

35:13.740 --> 35:21.000
So, yeah, 276 solves all three of these, all three of the given congruences here in example 9 at once.

35:22.160 --> 35:23.920
And, that is the Chinese Remainder Theorem.

35:24.980 --> 35:26.100
It's not really that bad.

35:27.120 --> 35:29.880
